**F3 — Economy**: ore→metal (forge consumes `ore`+`power`), ash→soil→food (greenhouse two-stage in `doProduction`); caps enforced and overflow logged in `addResource`/`logOverflow`. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonists have `skill`,`fatigue`,`morale`,`job`,`assignedBuildingId`; `skillFactor(c.skill)` and `computeMoraleFatigueFactor(c)` read directly in `doProduction`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `resolveNeeds` consumes food/water per colonist; shortage calls `adjustAllMorale(s,-5)`; morale feeds `computeMoraleFatigueFactor` into production; recovery via `fatigue<50` morale regen and rest. Score 2.

**F6 — Research**: 10 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `researchPrereqsMet` enforced in `tryResearch`; costs deducted via `payCost`; each unlock either gates a building (`isBuildingUnlocked`) or applies a real multiplier read in `doProduction`/`resolveHazard`. Score 2.

**F7 — Events**: 13 entries in `EVENTS`; `rngWeighted` selection; 5 choice-events with 2 options each with differing `apply()` state changes; `eventCooldowns` set and decremented in `resolveHazard`. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade**: `resolveTrade` computes buy/sell price from `stockRatio` and drifting `market.drift[g]` (random walk each caravan); `caravan.inventory[].qty` limited and decremented; `tradeBuy`/`tradeSell` both implemented and wired to UI buttons. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: `resolveHazard` fires every 6 turns (`s.turn % 6`); `severity` grows with `Math.floor(s.turn/12)`; damaged buildings check `b.hp<=0`→`disabled` and production skips disabled/dead buildings (`if(b.disabled||b.hp<=0) return;`); `storm_walls`/`reinforced_housing` research reduce damage; `repairBuilding` spends parts and restores hp/clears disabled. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serializeState` → JSON text into textarea; `deserializeState` validates required fields, array lengths, rng shape, throws descriptive `Error`s shown in `#loadmsg`. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: `checkEndConditions` has both win (`alive>=12 && needsMet` at turn 60) and lose (`alive.length===0`, or turn 60 without win) branches, both reachable; `computeScore` uses population/research/turn/stockpile; `checkGameOverOverlay` renders summary screen. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab` wires nav buttons; log entries carry `[T'+e.turn+']`; tooltips via `data-tip`/`title` attached widely (`tip()`, `attachTooltipEvents`); keyboard shortcuts (`Space`, `1`-`5`) in `keydown` listener; `@media (max-width:500px)` responsive CSS. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests` has 18 assertions on real invariants (cap enforcement, prereq gating, save/load hash equality, assignment consistency, RNG determinism, clamping); `runBenchmark` runs a headless greedy policy loop up to 200 turns without DOM and returns `hashState` result. Score 2.

**G1 — research→yield**: `efficient_chains.mult` read as `chainMult` in `doProduction` (forge & greenhouse); `advanced_filtration.mult` read as `condMult` for condenser; `vent_tapping` gates generator existence. Full chain traced, applied every relevant turn. Score 4.

**G2 — shortfall→morale→output**: `resolveNeeds` computes `foodShort`/`waterShort` → `adjustAllMorale(s,-5)`; `computeMoraleFatigueFactor` reads `c.morale` and multiplies into every production formula (`mf`). Fully wired, every turn. Score 4.

**G3 — storm→damage→output loss→repair→recovery**: `resolveHazard` reduces `b.hp`, sets `b.disabled` at 0 hp; production skips `b.disabled||b.hp<=0` entirely (binary loss, not gradual, but real output loss); `repairBuilding` spends parts (`Math.ceil(missing/5)`), restores hp and `disabled=false`. Minor gap: partial damage (hp reduced but >0) does NOT reduce output at all — only full disable stops production, so a building at 90% damage still produces at full rate. Score 3.

**G4 — trade prices vs stockpile/supply**: `resolveTrade` buy/sell price formulas read `stockRatio = resources[g]/caps[g]` and multiply by `market.drift[g]`, which is updated via random walk each caravan turn. Score 4.

**G5 — event choices mutate state**: `migrants` choice: welcome adds colonists via `addColonist`+resource cost vs turn-away adds scrip — both mutate different state; `sickness` choice: quarantine costs food/water+morale vs ignore has RNG-branched morale hit — different state paths, not just log text. Score 4.

